{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Take the Levites from among the children of Israel.</b> The section of the Levites is juxtaposed to the section of the Menorah because the Menorah was a commandment entrusted to the priests; therefore He juxtaposed to it this section, which is the commandment of the Levites — that they begin their service — and after it, the commandment of the Paschal offering, which is a commandment incumbent upon all Israel. This is what it says (Numbers 9:2): ״ויעשו בני ישראל את הפסח״, and if so, the sections are arranged with great providence in the ordering of the ranks: priest, and after him Levite, and after him Israel. And it says קח את הלוים מתוך וגו׳ — 'Take the Levites from among…' — because they were intermingled at Mount Sinai, and so too all the tribes before they set out on the way."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:30:43.834553084Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}